  "method": "Pacific Electric: Wikipedia route maps where a line has one; the Long Beach-San Pedro, Hawthorne-El Nido and Westgate lines traced on USGS 1:24,000 sheets of 1924-25; in central Los Angeles every rail line drawn solid red on the Pacific Electric engineering department's 1927 map (C.E. 8214), extracted by colour, its motor coach (bus) lines left out by their dashes; elsewhere the lines traced from the 1925 Kelker, De Leuw plate and snapped to surviving rail or road centrelines, and OpenHistoricalMap track where the plate agrees. Los Angeles Railway: each line routed on today's streets from the street sequence its Wikipedia article gives for the 1920s, checked against the 1927 map, plus every other line drawn solid yellow on that map. The layer shows the networks about 1925; the central lines are as of 1927. Route miles: lines buffered 25 m and unioned, shared track counted once, per company.",
